[{:db/id 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125062 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-10$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ has algebraic multiplicity $3$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558" :question/id #uuid "970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558" :question/math-academy-id "q-37356" :question/problem "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $B$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =-5$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )((3-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )+10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +3)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7$, we have that the only real eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-3$ (both with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24804dcb-504d-588f-82a7-fb6fe2bd5e63"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24804dcb-504d-588f-82a7-fb6fe2bd5e63" :answer-field/id #uuid "24804dcb-504d-588f-82a7-fb6fe2bd5e63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95f7c606-fabc-51e1-8528-9632cdd50f62" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c80a4f86-8e3e-57b3-9a46-45e60e433bf6" "answer-95f7c606-fabc-51e1-8528-9632cdd50f62" "answer-0069a32c-24a8-592d-aebc-701756d8bdcd" "answer-8e52e58b-8a75-5be5-b33c-025f9395fdc7" "answer-f29dc51e-2c92-5c6d-8ac3-24dd5e961743"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c80a4f86-8e3e-57b3-9a46-45e60e433bf6" :answer/id #uuid "c80a4f86-8e3e-57b3-9a46-45e60e433bf6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95f7c606-fabc-51e1-8528-9632cdd50f62" :answer/id #uuid "95f7c606-fabc-51e1-8528-9632cdd50f62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0069a32c-24a8-592d-aebc-701756d8bdcd" :answer/id #uuid "0069a32c-24a8-592d-aebc-701756d8bdcd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e52e58b-8a75-5be5-b33c-025f9395fdc7" :answer/id #uuid "8e52e58b-8a75-5be5-b33c-025f9395fdc7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f29dc51e-2c92-5c6d-8ac3-24dd5e961743" :answer/id #uuid "f29dc51e-2c92-5c6d-8ac3-24dd5e961743" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2" :question/id #uuid "bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-140475" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )+(-5-\\lambda )+(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $10:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 5,\\pm 10\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-13(1)+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-13$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d8e6f41c-9e5c-55de-9517-8eaa2b14ab20"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d8e6f41c-9e5c-55de-9517-8eaa2b14ab20" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e6f41c-9e5c-55de-9517-8eaa2b14ab20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1d0700ae-412d-51b3-a257-618c99674341" "answer-6819477a-eb82-5fe8-9144-a2c3b8ccd8c0" "answer-974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" "answer-481860b5-bb3d-58cb-94dc-529c4d401e99" "answer-558359c6-2d82-546e-a690-6c2a868d98cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d0700ae-412d-51b3-a257-618c99674341" :answer/id #uuid "1d0700ae-412d-51b3-a257-618c99674341" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-2,1,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6819477a-eb82-5fe8-9144-a2c3b8ccd8c0" :answer/id #uuid "6819477a-eb82-5fe8-9144-a2c3b8ccd8c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,-1,2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer/id #uuid "974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-481860b5-bb3d-58cb-94dc-529c4d401e99" :answer/id #uuid "481860b5-bb3d-58cb-94dc-529c4d401e99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-558359c6-2d82-546e-a690-6c2a868d98cc" :answer/id #uuid "558359c6-2d82-546e-a690-6c2a868d98cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,2,5\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-3b7302f6-4f44-5e74-82d2-2ea10325bde3" :activity/id #uuid "3b7302f6-4f44-5e74-82d2-2ea10325bde3" :activity/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050376 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-4407ab4d-760d-5929-a4aa-ceca8bb19594" "step-34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" "step-e50043bb-5fa2-5c1d-b766-cd5b3092a18e" "step-41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" "step-3399fe8e-8176-5e35-93d5-9a34329ea9c3"] :activity/first-step "step-4407ab4d-760d-5929-a4aa-ceca8bb19594" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-4407ab4d-760d-5929-a4aa-ceca8bb19594" :step/id #uuid "4407ab4d-760d-5929-a4aa-ceca8bb19594" :step/content 17592186125062 :step/next "step-34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" :step/id #uuid "34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" :step/content "question-970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558" :step/next "step-e50043bb-5fa2-5c1d-b766-cd5b3092a18e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e50043bb-5fa2-5c1d-b766-cd5b3092a18e" :step/id #uuid "e50043bb-5fa2-5c1d-b766-cd5b3092a18e" :step/content 17592186323910 :step/next "step-41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" :step/id #uuid "41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" :step/content "question-bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2" :step/next "step-3399fe8e-8176-5e35-93d5-9a34329ea9c3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3399fe8e-8176-5e35-93d5-9a34329ea9c3" :step/id #uu